Minecraft is probably one of the reasons I'm into tech today.

I started playing Minecraft when I was around 10 years old. At first, it was just a game I loved playing.

But as I got older, I became more curious about what was happening behind the game.

I started experimenting with Minecraft servers, plugins, configurations, and eventually server development.

I remember spending hours trying to figure out why something wasn't working, searching for solutions, changing things, breaking them, and trying again.

Looking back, I think that was one of my first experiences with actually learning through building and experimenting.

It wasn't a coding course or a textbook that got me interested in technology.

It was Minecraft.

And now, years later, I'm studying Information Technology, building websites, working on my own businesses, and even making my portfolio Minecraft themed.

Funny how things come full circle. 🎮

#Minecraft #Technology #WebDevelopment #Programming #Learning #BuildInPublic
